From 3c8e08f1faee23b3965273b842cf11d6d25d6617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:40:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] device: consume built-in custom keys and isolate gesture
 repeats

Page-key actions (folded from 0002-add-page-key-actions): page_up and page_down are appended to the screen-on button action list; they inject a standard PAGE_UP/PAGE_DOWN key into the focused window.

A page key whose UP injection is not accepted is released with a cancelled UP (immediately, else on the next page action or service interrupt/destroy), so the key never stays pressed.

The overlay-permission prompt on a key press is removed: the app runs as the system uid (overlay permission always granted) and the panel is an accessibility overlay.
